# .env.example
#
# Nothing in this folder needs a key to run. The page reads JSON files that are
# already beside it, the tests read the same files, and the scripts only listen
# on a local port.
#
# Real values for a WordPress application password, an SMTP login or an API key
# belong in .env (ignored), or better, in .local/ which is ignored as well. They
# are never committed and never pasted into data/*.json — those files are
# published.
#
# If a key does appear in a file that git carries, rotate it first and clean up
# second. Removing the commit does not un-leak it.
